{
  "$comment": "Parameter normalization cases (方案 §5.2, E-07, E-08). Pure function normalize(profile, request) → aspect / resolution / quality / wire body keys (dotted) / batches / adjustments. Every route and every sizeParam of image_profile.v2.json has at least one case (reverse gate). request.aspect null means the user picked nothing; the wire still carries an explicit ratio (explicitAspect.defaultAspect). adjustments are what the UI shows in the blue notice bar. Algorithm: aspect = nearest by |ln ratio| (ties keep the earlier list entry); resolution = highest available tier not above the request, else the lowest; wxh: long edge = resolutions[tier], short edge from the ratio, each rounded to the nearest multipleOf, then clamp maxLongEdge → maxPixels (floor) → minPixels (ceil); n > maxNPerCall splits; nParam false sends n single requests; a quality tier missing from qualityMap is never sent. Result is either the normalized object or {error: invalid_profile | invalid_request} (P5·U4a ruling), profile checked first: a request value that is set but outside the closed set (aspect not W:H with sides 1-9999 and no leading zero, tier not 1K/2K/4K, quality not draft/standard/fine, n not a positive integer; n = 0 counts as unset) is invalid_request; a profile with an empty or malformed aspectRatios, maxNPerCall < 1, or no available tier is invalid_profile. null / missing / empty string all mean unset; unset request fields take defaults and never produce adjustments. Tier tables are read per entry: a qualityMap or resolutionValues entry that is not a non-empty string is a missing tier (for aspect_resolution / gemini_image_config a tier needs both resolutions and resolutionValues); sizeConstraints is read per sub-field (non-positive-integer = absent, multipleOf defaults to 1). nParam missing or null = true. Size adjustments always write WxH. After every size step each edge is at least one multipleOf. maxLongEdge clamp uses integer math floor(edge * maxLongEdge / longEdge / multipleOf) * multipleOf. Executable reference: scripts/lib/studio-image-reference.mjs normalizeParams.",
